    {
      "id": "claim_0c82ebc7d1034866819595bf0e9189c1",
      "statement": "Operationally, a Florida decision must first identify the policy and attached endorsement effective at the date of loss, then separate underwriting or renewal evidence from covered-loss causation, apply the contract's roof valuation and deductible provisions, and verify the applicable notice, disclosure, claim, and deadline rules; applying the wrong edition or treating age, a bulletin, or an internal underwriting decision as a coverage determination is a failure mode.",
